Root cause:
The bug was caused by not clearing the old URLContext pointer (`hd`) when closing the connection in scenarios involving authentication or redirects. This could lead to the reuse of a stale or invalid pointer, resulting in issues when attempting to open HTTP URLs that require authentication or handle redirects. The patch addresses this by explicitly setting the pointer to `NULL` after closing the connection, ensuring that subsequent operations do not mistakenly use an outdated reference.
